{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989332-mage-the-awakening-renaissance-era","id":989332,"title":"Mage the Awakening - Renaissance Era","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-18T07:12:41-07:00","id":989332,"title":"Mage the Awakening - Renaissance Era","content":"Hi folks, so I'm doing my due diligence on researching Venice during the Renaissance, in no small part inspired by recently reading Sorcerer's Crusade. However, with my players preferring ChroD's take on the mechanics of being a Mage, and not having that K at the end of the word magic, I'm trying to work out some guidelines for my setting. Now, I've read the majority of first edition material for Mage, and have digested the mechanics of second (and the majority of the setting lore), but my mind is a sieve overly full of random stuff to keep sense of everything.<br /> <br /> So, rambling and meandering introduction out of the way, I'll come to some kind of point. I'm curious about two things and would love to hear about any ideas or answers to these. The first is, what canonical material do we have about mages in the Renaissance period, around the 1460s and on. For example, I know that the Adamantine Arrow had formed by the point To the Strongest occurs, so they exist. I also know DaveB said that the Silver Ladder formed around the second century, so both of those exist within the setting, but the great refusal is quite a ways off, so no FreeCs yet. So, if you've got any tidbits mentioned in some of the books, please feel free to enlighten me about the period as presented in Awakening. <br /> <br /> Secondly, I would love to know if anyone has done any work towards this themselves, recently or in the past. If so, I'd love to hear what you've done. I'd also love to hear any ideas on modifying Awakenings Orders and Ministries to something resembling the dichotomy of the Traditions and Order of Reason. Of course I can come up with a lot of this all on my lonesome, but other sources of ideas are always very welcome during these proto-planning out sections of any chronicles creation.<br /> <br /> Edit: Testing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 10-23-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:53:52-07:00","id":989369,"title":"","content":"I also loved <b>Sorcerer's Crusade</b> of <b>Ascension</b> - would love to have this period in <b>Awakening</b> to run!<br /> <br /> Renaissance Era is proposed <b>Dark Era</b> for <b>Mage</b> ( maybe in <b>DE </b>2? ) as by official materials, it was time of Seers of Throne reform, when they changed from separate cults into modern Ministries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989332-mage-the-awakening-renaissance-era#post989332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, rambling and meandering introduction out of the way, I'll come to some kind of point. I'm curious about two things and would love to hear about any ideas or answers to these. The first is, what canonical material do we have about mages in the Renaissance period, around the 1460s and on. For example, I know that the Adamantine Arrow had formed by the point To the Strongest occurs, so they exist. I also know DaveB said that the Silver Ladder formed around the second century, so both of those exist within the setting, but the great refusal is quite a ways off, so no FreeCs yet. So, if you've got any tidbits mentioned in some of the books, please feel free to enlighten me about the period as presented in Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened\">History of Awakened</a> fan timeline, based on various 1E and <b>Dark Eras</b> books. It's closest we have to history of the Awakening compiled before <b>Tome of Pentacle</b>. I tried to as faithful to official books as can be.<br /> <br /> What we know is that at Alexander's the Great times there are <i>no</i> Orders. yet, only various Darshanas cults around world. And by 1st BCE we have all Diamond Orders, as Guardians are running from Rome before Seers of Throne secret Empire emerging. Also, until 12th AD we have two Orders instead one Mysterium. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At 15th Century, first Ministry - Hegemony - is created from Seers cults of Unity.<br /> <br /> A little quote from <b>Seers of Throne</b> book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seers of Throne, p. 56-57</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The modern Ministry formed in Western Europe during the 15th century. The early Renaissance provided fertile ground for the Unity\u2019s cult \u2014 several cults, in fact. These pylons let Italian city-states fight their battles for them. Florence, Milan and Venice prevailed. <br /> At the dawn of the 16th century, Seers from each city met and formed L\u2019Hegemonie Secr\u00e8te (French was the language of the elite at the time) and from there followed traders, explorers and conquerors to the rest of the world, absorbing rival Unity worshipers as soon as they found them. Two centuries later, L\u2019Hegemonie shifted its main strength to England and the Americas, and reached the height of power, going so far as to reshape other Seer factions in the image of the British Empire and the burgeoning Masonic societies of the colonies. A Ministry is called a Ministry today because of the hegemons; they never tire of pointing it out.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/989332-mage-the-awakening-renaissance-era#post989332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, I would love to know if anyone has done any work towards this themselves, recently or in the past. If so, I'd love to hear what you've done. I'd also love to hear any ideas on modifying Awakenings Orders and Ministries to something resembling the dichotomy of the Traditions and Order of Reason. Of course I can come up with a lot of this all on my lonesome, but other sources of ideas are always very welcome during these proto-planning out sections of any chronicles creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>At 15th Century there are <i>no</i> Ministry yet. They all are various Iron Seals cults, becoming slowly Ministries from mixing up. Probably some Archmasters Seers become first Ministers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-18-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:10:31-07:00","id":989381,"title":"","content":"And, well, as <b>Assassin's Creed</b> fan I can only point to ready-made 'great Guardians-Seers War' plotline on three games of series. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>AC</b> works as marvelous inspiration for <b>MtAw</b>, as secrets societies of it are almost the Orders from <b>Mage</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lZPQ2ijCgVw\" data-code=\"lZPQ2ijCgVw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lZPQ2ijCgVw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:47:07-07:00","id":989405,"title":"","content":"Also, consider the rise of mercenary companies that fight for the powerful Italian city-states of the time as the seed for a later schism within the Adamantine Arrow. Constant conflict or honorable causes? The rise of mercenary companies of Arrows would later see a counter-movement in the form of the Code Duello and the idealization of single combat. <br /> <br /> Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T10:22:55-07:00","id":989421,"title":"","content":"If you want to prefigure some of the conflicts that happen again in the Nameless War, you could represent the Order of Reason or a similar group as a widespread and innovative Nameless Order. The fun thing about the shared Atlantean cosmology of both Seers and Diamond is pitting both of them against a group that has fundamentally different ideas about magic and the Supernal World that still <i>work. </i>Picture a brief and unsteady alliance between the nascent Ministry of Hegemony and the Silver Ladder against a mutual threat to their cults and cryptopolies in a sphere that the Renaissance humanists threaten, or the Mysterium working furiously to keep the Order of Reason from destroying magic via pancryptia by exposing it to Sleepers for study.<br /> <br /> If you want something evoking the Traditions/Order of Reason conflict, consider using the Thrice-Great as a prominent Legacy in the setting. This is the period when their classical astrology is being challenged by scientific advancement and they start to lose some temporal and mystical power when it becomes clear that their Truths aren't actually accurate.<br /> <br /> Something to consider from a uniquely Awakening standpoint: there was <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?658166-Mage-the-Awakening-I-read-a-Legacy-a-day\" target=\"_blank\">a thread on RPGnet</a> a few years ago where the OP read and reviewed every published Legacy, and drew some interesting insights about the implied setting from them that wasn't necessarily intended by any one writer. One was that many Legacies claim to originate in Renaissance Italy, whereas others claimed to be founded in some numinous and non-empirical &quot;right after the Fall&quot; time, and from that the OP imagined a setting where the fall of Atlantis (accounting for its Time warping effects, colloquially called Last Tuesdayism) had occurred just a few years before the Renaissance.<br /> <br /> found the quote:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, if you want a Last Tuesdayist mindfuck in your game, I think there is excellent background for Renaissance Italy as the remnants of the wreckage of Atlantis and the dawn of the post-Fall world (or at least this iteration of it). It's full of ruins of more impressive times, squalid with hints of splendor, and generally speaking a Legacy originating before it is either allegedly pre-Fall or &quot;established just after the Fall so we're really old, honest.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> One thing the Tremere have in common with the Tremere Revisited is the idea that they are part of the hidden history of the Middle Ages. (If Renaissance Italy was the dawn of the post-Fall world, the Tremere could be the shadow of a late development in Atlantis related to the causes of the Fall.) </div> </div> </div>Some Legacies that claim to originate in the Renaissance: Stewards of the Celestial Orrery, Chrysalides, Architects of the Future, Celestial Masters. Between the founding of the Ministry of Hegemony and several of their Legacies, this period seems like a golden age for the Seers with lots of creativity and magical innovation in the service of human misery. Something to think about!<br /> <br /> random NPC concept: Thyrsus proto-biologist in the Order of Reason, looking for insight into human politics and city-state conflict by studying the migration of birds and the organization of ants and bees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-18-2016, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:07:54-07:00","id":989441,"title":"","content":"Also, the Mysterium has some factions within itself that hold some fairly misanthropic views on Sleepers and Sleepers societies. At the same time, they have the time-honored mandate of promoting knowledge and scholarship among the Sleeper populace. Before, the Church was the main institution spearheading the gathering of knowledge, I imagine that many Athenea of the time had developed after the monastic traditions of Christianity. But the wars in the Eastern Roman Empire, the Reconquista in Spain and the new trade routes made by the Portuguese brought an unprecedented influx of people, treasures and new ideas. While some of that influence favored a revisitation of the knowledge from the Classical period, many advances in mathematics, astronomy, medicine were recent developments that only now had started to reach Western Europe. For a mystagogue, the Natural world can never be understood through Reason alone (out the sacred triad of Reason, Tradition and Gnosis), but at least it's a start. And an educated population perhaps can strengthen the symbolic power the order stands for, giving it primacy over this new age. As a faction within the Mysterium, the Illuminated Ones would try to foster proper scholarship and education at a level appropriate to each person's degree of enlightenment.<br /> What could happen when the nascent &quot;Order of Reason&quot; tries to blatantly dismiss Tradition in favor of Reason? What would happen when their attempts to Awaken Sleepers through scientific inspiration backfires and worsens Pancryptia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T00:15:07-07:00","id":989758,"title":"","content":"I ran a game, briefly, set in Asti in the 1350s. This is noteworthy, because 1350 was the year the Black Death was noted to have settled.<br /> You might check out this: <a href=\"http://dailyhistory.org/How_did_the_Bubonic_Plague_make_the_Italian_Renaissance_possible%3F\" target=\"_blank\">http://dailyhistory.org/How_did_the_Bubonic_Plague_make_the_Italian_Renais sance_possible</a> <br /> <br /> The way I went with it was that a lot of reapers flourished, taking souls from the vast pool of already condemned. Vampire's used it as cover for their predation, but had drastically reduced herds, which drove them into competition.<br /> <br /> The Elemental Masters were a significant force in the region, though the diamond still insisted on calling them Nameless. <br /> <br /> Of course, the entire country was rife with intrigue already by then. IRL, That was around the same time (1345) that queen Joan of Naples had her husband murdered. (or simply happened to benefit from it, depending who you believe.) Interesting tidbit: Andrew's mom gave him a magic ring that would protect him from poison or stabbing... so they strangled him and defenestrated him.<br /> <br /> Wars between nobles were already common and heating up. While not all the same houses were players that late Renaissance had, this would be around the time they were growing and the intrigues were already underway. Certain merchant families gained fortune that last to the present. The rise of the families that would fight over the papacy itself is here, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure just what sorts of details you seek, but there are some general sweeping themes to play with, especially in the early days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:45:39-07:00","id":989850,"title":"","content":"i would suggest to restric your work on a few themes to avoid creating a too much complex setting. Rinascimento was full of events, it was a time of change in every aspect of society and much conflict happened, intrigues and politics were incredibly complex considering that society wasn't structured in &quot;nations&quot; or &quot;states&quot; and factions came from different backgrounds and levels of society all scheming for power and glory. The church was funding universities and art but was also fightining against &quot;new ideas&quot; that found fertile ground in the same places, to make things even more complex the schism was just ended by the council of costance and the curch was dealing with the consequences trying to streghten its position in the empire (the curch considered itself an imperial institution) and at the same time affirm the predominance of the pope on the emperor.<br /> <br /> In the east the ottoman empire conquered constantinople destroying the eastern roman empire and closing the routes to china and india damaging genova and venezia greatly, in the north a few years after the end of the 100 years war england is engulfed in the war of the two roses, frence starts a series of profound changes trying to reunite under one banner and trying to rebuild a kingdom, in the iberic peninsula the reconquista destoryes the tolerant islamic kingdom.<br /> To complicate the matter columbus discovers the west indies and the repubbliche marinare of northern italy are going to see the start of their decline as commerce moves from the mediterranean sea to the atlantic while the powerfull banker families thrive and the comuni become so strong to challenge even imperial authority and to claim a de facto autonomy.<br /> <br /> In such complex time i would try to identify a few conflicts to focus on and from there find who could be involved: for ex. i can imagine the conflict between universities as a fertile ground for the conflict between progressive mages and traditionalists, or between some factions in the orders and the seers or even mixing things where some seers are &quot;allied&quot; with some atlantean order factions. Silver ladder could be behind some powerfull merchant families promoting humanist ideas (for ex. the perfect city) and financing art, while the seers could be acting behind the roman curia to defeat the new ideas, in the mean time guardians could be working inside imperial structures. You could even depict a completly chaotic setting where everyone is enemy of everyone else and at the same time allied, silver ladder could be promoting humanist ideas but only the ones that are compatible to neo platonism while the seers could be promoting neo platonism to avoid the birth of new ideas...<br /> <br /> anyway i reapet: choose a few themes and events you want to focus on, this way is surely easier to manage the thing and would be easier to recive inputs too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7038-nirgal","name":"Nirgal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:01:01-07:00","id":989876,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree with limiting my theme and idea pool here. Reading up on the Renaissance, there are a million things going on, all of interest and great import, and that's before even considering the shadowy ChroD material going on in the backgrounds. As mentioned above, I'm going to focus on Venice as my main playground so I'm thinking of focusing on a mix of the conflict between Venice and the Ottomon, and the nascent forming of the Hegemonic ministry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}